cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this replication package, please cite the paper it accompanies
  (see preferred-citation below). Cite the software itself only if you use the
  estimation code independently of the paper.

title: >-
  HMM-Decentralised-Perpetual-Futures: replication package for Same Formula,
  Different Signal: Funding-Rate Censoring and the Premium Gap between
  Hyperliquid and Centralised Perpetuals
abstract: >-
  Code, data and fitted parameters for a comparison of funding-rate censoring
  on the Hyperliquid, Binance and Bybit BTC and ETH perpetuals, from October
  2025 to April 2026 and from December 2023 to September 2026; the
  hour-by-hour premium gap between Hyperliquid and the exchanges, with its
  Shapley decomposition; a two-state Markov-switching AR(1) on the premium
  with Hessian, OPG and sandwich inference and the multi-start protocol its
  multi-modal likelihood requires; and a three-state Gaussian hidden Markov
  model on hourly returns, with the evidence on its boundary transition.
type: software
